doc:cbDiagnosticDecisionConfiguration opmad:has_text_value "A CB is normal if and only if all acoustic signal-processing tests are fulfilled; failure of any test yields an abnormal diagnosis. Only an acoustic signal is required for CB testing; current signal processing is not required. To declare a CB normal, signatures acquired from that CB under similar conditions must consistently yield normal results." .
